<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The guns: a Mk 15 Phalanx on a 3 m stack node, a 5"/54 Mk 42 mount and an M197 chin turret. None
  carries a missile, so each declares no <Tube> and fires through its GunMunition alone. Part
  definitions are in ../KSArmory*.xml, which KSA reads and this does not.
-->
<WeaponPack Schema="1" Family="Guns">

  <!--
    The M61A2's 20 mm round, fired by both the Phalanx and the M197. LaunchSpeed, MaxRange and the
    102 g mass are the real round's.

    FuseRadius="2.5" is ours, not the real round's: a real 20 mm round has to hit. The mod checks for
    contact in small time steps, and at 1100 m/s a radius smaller than 2.5 m can fall between two of
    them and be missed.

    MaxFlightSeconds="2.5": a shell takes 2.1 s to reach the gun's 1486 m range, so it is removed just
    after. Longer costs frame time: the gun fires 75 rounds a second, so every extra second of life is
    75 more shells to step and draw. TracerBurnSeconds="2.2" ends the glow just before the shell is
    removed, so the stream fades out rather than being cut off.
  -->
  <Munition Name="20MM" DisplayName="M61A2 20 mm"
            MinRange="100" MaxRange="1486"
            LaunchSpeed="1100" BoostSeconds="0" BoostAccel="0" MaxFlightSeconds="2.5"
            MassKg="0.102" CalibreMm="20" DragCoefficient="0.3"
            FuseRadius="2.5" FuseArmSeconds="0.03" ChargeKg="0.05"
            TracerEvery="4" TracerBurnSeconds="2.2" />

  <!--
    The 5"/54's anti-aircraft shell. LaunchSpeed and the 3.3 kg charge are the real round's; MaxRange is
    how far out the mount engages.

    TimedFuse="true": the shell bursts at the flight time the aiming solution asked for, so it does not
    have to hit. Its charge gives about 11 m of lethal radius (the 20 mm's is 2.7 m). A target that
    manoeuvres after the shot is missed by however far it moved. If the shell does touch a craft first,
    it bursts there. MinRange is the distance at which the fuze has armed.

    DragCoefficient="0.306" with the real 31.75 kg at 127 mm reproduces the range table's 23.69 km at
    47 degrees. One constant cannot also match the real ceiling: fired straight up it reaches 16.1 km
    against the real 14.8, because real drag peaks near Mach 1.

    MaxFlightSeconds="120" is a safety timeout, not the flight time. A shell whose path can only end on
    the ground has no timeout at all and is removed when it lands (RoundReach); the 120 s only removes a
    shell whose path cannot be classified.

    HitsTerrain="true" makes the ground stop the shell; without it, a shell that misses falls through the
    planet. It costs one terrain lookup per shell per frame, which is affordable because at 40 rounds a
    minute only a few dozen are ever in the air.
  -->
  <Munition Name="5IN54" DisplayName="5&quot;/54 HEDP"
            BodyModel="KSArmory_Mk42Shell_SubPart" BodyLength="0.42825"
            MinRange="350" MaxRange="15700"
            LaunchSpeed="807.7" BoostSeconds="0" BoostAccel="0" MaxFlightSeconds="120"
            MassKg="31.75" CalibreMm="127" DragCoefficient="0.306"
            TimedFuse="true" FuseRadius="12" FuseArmSeconds="0.45" ChargeKg="3.3"
            HitsTerrain="true" />

  <!--
    The Phalanx's search and track radar, in the radome above the gun. Short-ranged and wide, because a
    CIWS is the last line of defence and has to see everything close, quickly.

    ConeDeg="115" reaches down to the mount's own -25 degrees: a missile skimming in low stays under
    5 degrees of elevation until the last few hundred metres, which is too late to start aiming.
  -->
  <Sensor Name="VPS2" DisplayName="VPS-2 search and track" Scope="Search"
          Range="6000" ConeDeg="115"
          ThreatRadius="2500" ThreatHorizonSeconds="15" LockSeconds="0.6"
          Emits="true" />

  <!--
    The Mk 68 director that aims the 5"/54. Range="18000" is past the gun's 15.7 km reach on purpose: a
    shell takes over twenty seconds to get there, so the target has to be tracked well before the first
    one is fired. ConeDeg="105" reaches down to the mount's own -15 degrees.
  -->
  <Sensor Name="MK68" DisplayName="Mk 68 fire control" Scope="Search"
          Range="18000" ConeDeg="105"
          ThreatRadius="15700" ThreatHorizonSeconds="30" LockSeconds="1.2"
          Emits="true" />

  <!--
    The chin turret's sight. Optical, so it emits nothing. BoresightSource="MountNormal" points it out of
    the mounting face, which on a chin turret is down; ConeDeg="100" covers the gun's whole travel,
    which reaches 10 degrees past the face's plane.
  -->
  <Sensor Name="TSU" DisplayName="Telescopic sight unit"
          Range="8000" ConeDeg="100" BoresightSource="MountNormal"
          ThreatRadius="2000" ThreatHorizonSeconds="20" LockSeconds="0.6"
          MinTargetSpeed="0" />

  <!--
    Mk 15 Phalanx. The housing traverses and the barrels elevate; there is no missile launcher, so no
    PodsMarker. The pivots and muzzles are taken from the Blender export.

    Elevation is the real mount's -25 to +85. The real mount is also limited to 150 degrees either side,
    to keep the barrels off a ship's superstructure; on a stack node nothing is behind it, and the mod's
    own travel map keeps the barrels off the craft it is on, so no TraverseLimitDeg is set.

    SearchRadarRpm="90" only drives the radar scope's sweep; nothing on the model spins (NavWeaps).
    GunRoundMassKg="0.26": one 20 x 102 mm cartridge; the part's 6,200 kg includes a full magazine.
    ReloadSeconds="0": it has no missile tubes, so a reload timer would never stop.
  -->
  <Launcher PartId="KSArmory_Prefab_Ciws" DisplayName="Mk 15 Phalanx"
            FireControlLabel="Mk 15 fire control"
            Munition="20MM" Sensor="VPS2"
            TurretMarker="Ciws_Turret" GunsMarker="Ciws_Guns"
            TurretPivot="0.80000, 0.00000, 0.00000" GunPivotFromTurret="1.45000, 0.00000, 0.00000"
            GunMunition="20MM"
            SlewRateDeg="100" ElevationRateDeg="86"
            MinElevationDeg="-25" MaxElevationDeg="85" ForwardMinElevationDeg="-25"
            SettleSeconds="0.2" SearchRadarRpm="90"
            GunAmmo="1550" GunRoundMassKg="0.26" GunRoundsPerMinute="4500"
            GunBurstRounds="60" GunBurstGapSeconds="0.35" GunReloadSeconds="0"
            ReloadSeconds="0">
    <Muzzle At=" 0.07900, 2.15000,  0.00000" />
    <Muzzle At=" 0.04700, 2.15000,  0.05543" />
    <Muzzle At="-0.01700, 2.15000,  0.05543" />
    <Muzzle At="-0.04900, 2.15000,  0.00000" />
    <Muzzle At="-0.01700, 2.15000, -0.05543" />
    <Muzzle At=" 0.04700, 2.15000, -0.05543" />
  </Launcher>

  <!--
    5"/54 Mk 42 single enclosed mount: forty rounds a minute against the CIWS's 4,500, and 15 km of reach
    against 1.5. Modelled in Blender by Mallikas; the pivots are taken from his export, and no script
    can regenerate or check them.

    GunPivotFromTurret puts the trunnion forward of the traverse axis, as on the real gun house. Slew and
    elevation rates and the -15 to +85 limits are the real mount's. SearchRadarFaces="0": the Mk 68 tracks
    one target, so the scope draws no sweep. GunBurstRounds="1" with no gap makes one press fire one shell,
    and lets auto-engage fire at the gun's own 40 a minute. The recoil values only affect the drawing, and
    were set by eye against this model.
  -->
  <Launcher PartId="KSArmory_Prefab_Mk42" DisplayName="5&quot;/54 Mk 42"
            FireControlLabel="Mk 68 fire control"
            Munition="5IN54" Sensor="MK68"
            TurretMarker="Mk42_Turret" GunsMarker="Mk42_Cannon" GunBarrelMarker="Mk42_Barrel"
            TurretPivot="0.01664, 0.00000, 0.00000" GunPivotFromTurret="1.53777, 0.48097, 0.00000"
            GunMunition="5IN54"
            SlewRateDeg="40" ElevationRateDeg="25"
            MinElevationDeg="-15" MaxElevationDeg="85" ForwardMinElevationDeg="-15"
            SettleSeconds="0.4" SearchRadarFaces="0"
            GunAmmo="599" GunRoundsPerMinute="40" GunBurstRounds="1" GunBurstGapSeconds="0"
            GunReloadSeconds="0"
            GunRecoilMetres="0.30" GunRecoilSeconds="0.08" GunReturnSeconds="0.60"
            GunshotSoundId="KSArmoryMk42Gunshot"
            ReloadSeconds="0">
    <Muzzle At="0.00000, 4.18860, 0.00000" />
  </Launcher>

  <!--
    M197 three-barrel 20 mm cannon in a chin turret. It attaches under a nose and hangs, so the part's +X
    points down: positive elevation in its frame is the gun pointing down in the world, and negative is
    up toward the aircraft. Modelled in Blender by Mallikas; the pivots are taken from his export.

    MinElevationDeg="-10" is where the model's actuator rod meets its cylinder (the real turret raises
    the gun 20.5 degrees). TraverseLimitDeg="110" is the turret's travel either side of straight ahead.
    GunFeedRatio="0.2" turns the ammunition belt 10 degrees when the gun points 50 degrees down.
  -->
  <Launcher PartId="KSArmory_Prefab_M197" DisplayName="M197 chin turret"
            FireControlLabel="M97 turret fire control"
            Munition="20MM" Sensor="TSU"
            TurretMarker="M197_Yoke" GunsMarker="M197_Gun"
            GunCylinderMarker="M197_Cylinder" GunRodMarker="M197_Rod"
            GunFeedMarker="M197_Belt" GunRotorMarker="M197_Barrels"
            TurretPivot="0.00000, 0.00000, 0.00000" GunPivotFromTurret="0.33333, -0.10773, 0.00000"
            GunCylinderPinFromTurret="0.03220, 0.37308, 0.00000"
            GunRodPinFromTurret="0.33474, 0.37308, 0.00000"
            GunFeedPivotFromTurret="0.06094, -0.10319, 0.00000" GunFeedRatio="0.2"
            GunRotorPivotFromTurret="0.50611, 0.70256, 0.00000"
            GunMunition="20MM"
            SlewRateDeg="80" ElevationRateDeg="60"
            MinElevationDeg="-10" MaxElevationDeg="50" ForwardArcDeg="0" RestElevationDeg="0"
            TraverseLimitDeg="110" SettleSeconds="0.2" SearchRadarFaces="0"
            GunAmmo="750" GunRoundMassKg="0.26" GunRoundsPerMinute="730"
            GunBurstRounds="16" GunBurstGapSeconds="0.5" GunReloadSeconds="0"
            GunSoundId="KSArmoryM197"
            ReloadSeconds="0">
    <Muzzle At="0.07726, 2.63549,  0.00000" />
    <Muzzle At="0.22055, 2.63549, -0.08272" />
    <Muzzle At="0.22055, 2.63549,  0.08272" />
  </Launcher>

</WeaponPack>
